# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is **already fully installed and configured** in this project. No changes were necessary.

## Verification Steps Completed

### 1. Documentation Review
✅ Fetched latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
✅ Confirmed framework-specific requirements for Next.js App Router

### 2. Package Installation
✅ `@vercel/analytics` package is installed (version 2.0.1)
✅ Package is listed in dependencies in `package.json`
✅ Package manager: pnpm (v11.9.0)

### 3. Component Integration
✅ Analytics component properly imported in `app/layout.tsx`:
   - Import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Usage: `<Analytics />` component added inside `<body>` tag

### 4. Implementation Details
**File:** `web/app/layout.tsx`
**Implementation:** Following Next.js App Router best practices from Vercel docs
```typescript
export default function RootLayout({ children }: LayoutProps<"/">) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={`dark ${sans.variable} ${mono.variable} antialiased`}>
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

### 5. Build & Testing
✅ Build completed successfully (`pnpm build`)
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ 40 pages generated successfully
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing errors in `.source` directory are pre-existing)

## Current Status
The project is ready to track analytics once deployed to Vercel. The Analytics component will:
- Automatically collect visitor data
- Track page views and web vitals
- Send data to Vercel Analytics dashboard
- Work seamlessly with Next.js App Router

## Next Steps (for project owner)
1. Deploy to Vercel (if not already deployed)
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
3. View analytics data after deployment at vercel.com/[your-project]/analytics

## Notes
- Implementation follows the latest Vercel documentation (as of November 11, 2026)
- Uses the recommended `@vercel/analytics/next` import for Next.js
- Component placement in root layout ensures tracking across all pages
- No additional configuration required
